Yg_9QdUj-yWiV-55g3io0Ooo18mJnlzDeyD8LEGpJMl8C1Pq0rrI82zzn6Jx5dO_edohw_QNGaA2ptOpzvtO1E1Z_w5P6dYc1sY1fAj_WbQ9y8NX95k5QmRVvec0040T-N20wXmYM1d1mGTynRBZ4qov\",\"width\":4032},{\"height\":3024,\"html_attributions\":[\"<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/maps.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/108682774657711399121\\\">L\\u2019 Angloy<\\/a>\"],\"photo_reference\":\"ATJ83zjPQjIuXAhDoBo3iCQ3_5MMOASrHT-FoazXmRAAaB7yODgTFTS7fPDXn4nHVUM8dOE8i15OjGGLxktxF9UbnQZ7qAJ7Us7AVO2P1rzr63iOEBBN0BrC0q4pm3Ndwg3uyBXfSwmXnYlF_1eQyPH3ndTgjkAxCs5XxGo14OyI8G9AMuWs\",\"width\":4032},{\"height\":4032,\"html_attributions\":[\"<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/maps.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/106360114523269968735\\\">Melanie Alfaro<\\/a>\"],\"photo_reference\":\"ATJ83zgxLdQE5zWDXOgmuTDqLoR4onJ6mzBqJHpBsSmz7GiB0JRwKhV_TttNc9opjhlSm2FDkI7RJBlWweu4SjDWQtJoecJNQnaS876-FHMKy9scZWleb6jMWx0YP9L6u2i6lfZJ3PwdVJoyBI5BbfTOeGMYrjjMCKKbN5vzHpACRj4_7G6q\",\"width\":3024},{\"height\":4032,\"html_attributions\":[\"<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/maps.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/118157065829271903470\\\">Jacob Kizer<\\/a>\"],\"photo_reference\":\"ATJ83zihwtufsMHLVrK7HyJ7ikyElsAu2qWVK9hN8SDu1TPfuPWwwgkh7VpgFgkJq6dzaJth2F0m6JMz5PZhPHav5u9Ak4TAnE2_PZEYwSF23Rwrh93xktdZ78A8k_poB4J30wUmdjpk-ExOeTRwousUFwEnyKxLpL58J70GyKaDtaBffVGV\",\"width\":3024},{\"height\":3024,\"html_attributions\":[\"<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/maps.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/105120419714212330752\\\">Mel anie<\\/a>\"],\"photo_reference\":\"ATJ83zimuFWu6E_gIvTg9ckW440yzNzsho-oFG7WBtFmTR-7m89G09K0hnAbBitnGEesNmu0icR9Ob8GG_L2-CmUWiArPwcfpVbIJplKbZdsqTTDiejtlN3cd57WIvksjRKR9atb0fO-bhb1L--XnHBCU4RGCWWeK335P-LnTnmsxXH8UFXD\",\"width\":4032}],\"place_id\":\"ChIJD9fgyEITM4cRgmZfywCMTdY\",\"plus_code\":{\"compound_code\":\"5WWW+XQ North Rim, AZ, USA\",\"global_code\":\"85895WWW+XQ\"},\"rating\":2.9,\"reference\":\"ChIJD9fgyEITM4cRgmZfywCMTdY\",\"reservable\":true,\"reviews\":[{\"author_name\":\"Jeremy K\",\"author_url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/108230324514200843843\\/reviews\",\"language\":\"en\",\"original_language\":\"en\",\"profile_photo_url\":\"https:\\/\\/lh3.googleusercontent.com\\/a-\\/ALV-UjWU2yreWyAlKrqYZ3NYGjH-ozrfFBesqFd-mGrSmpE2v1nH=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\",\"rating\":4,\"relative_time_description\":\"a month ago\",\"text\":\"The elk chili is delicious, with big tender chunks of meat and a bit of spice to it. I\'ve had it both on the hot dog and by itself, and been pleased both times. The pizza is fair if you manage your expectations--better than Little Caesars, but not by much. It\'s usually available across the way in the bar. Staff don\'t seem to know what\'s in or out of stock on a Sunday evening after the rush is over, and by the end of the day some of them were visibly burnt out.\\n\\nAvoid the brisket until they figure it out. The cook doesn\'t seem to realize that internal temp for brisket needs to reach around 200F for the connective tissue to really break down, and it\'s chewy to the point of being inedible. The waitstaff is aware of the problem, if you mention it.\",\"time\":1692110597,\"translated\":false},{\"author_name\":\"Peter \\u201cDizz\\u201d DISBURY\",\"author_url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/111378585556779676377\\/reviews\",\"language\":\"en\",\"original_language\":\"en\",\"profile_photo_url\":\"https:\\/\\/lh3.googleusercontent.com\\/a-\\/ALV-UjWaKmJtuDIKy0IyNH1r7jD63Aj4yPbhay8V9FlA4GFwfwc=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\",\"rating\":1,\"relative_time_description\":\"4 months ago\",\"text\":\"Was here several years ago and the food was bad then but it was to be expected.  Thankfully I did not pay for the meal my friend did and I just threw my food in the garbage.  The Pulled Pork sandwich had so much salt on it I think it could have killed a Bison.  After watching who was making the food it made sense.  My friend insisted on paying, I was much obliged not to eat the food.   Anytime the food has been saturated in salt that meal is shot, cannot resurrect it.\\nThe great thing with this experience is I did not eat here ever again.  On the South Rim there are much better food options and restaurants, the General Store there is great.\",\"time\":1684448040,\"translated\":false},{\"author_name\":\"Karen Fornof\",\"author_url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/103699293372919247029\\/reviews\",\"language\":\"en\",\"original_language\":\"en\",\"profile_photo_url\":\"https:\\/\\/lh3.googleusercontent.com\\/a\\/ACg8ocI41hOZVKpJUDHC7t7w0HeViPm_cq-NzQaLV8-o7vWV=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\",\"rating\":4,\"relative_time_description\":\"2 months ago\",\"text\":\"To be fair, this was their first full weekend being open and some of the food areas in the building were just becoming operational. The Deli is smack dab in the middle of grocery store shelves with drinks, snacks and fast food items. It seemed messy, crowded and sort of confusing before I took a moment to scope it out. So, I waited in a makeshift line at the deli counter and picked up some snacks for down the road. They had lots of amazing home baked cookies and pastries and the smell of fresh baked bread from their own in house bakery permeated the entire building. MMMmm so Good!\\n\\nAfter the Deli counter there\'s a lunch counter where I ordered the worst chicken tenders I\'ve ever had. They were served by two or three polite young men, who had just arrived there to work for the summer. They had no idea what they were doing yet, but they did whatever they could, willingly. They worked hard to please  and after all, it was their first day so no harsh judgement here. By now they probably have the preparation of those chicken tenders down pat and that was really the only thing that seriously needed fixing. To be fair, I won\'t be figuring those chicken tenders into the final star score.\\n\\nThere is also a sit down cafe\' in the building that we didn\'t try. I did, however, try the shopping, which was very fun with all sorts of beautiful hand made and Native American treasures. The prices were reasonable so I got some hand beaded 3 shield earrings. We also got gas here for a fair price. That\'s great since there\'s not many gas stations around and they could have easily gouged us... but they didn\'t.\",\"time\":1688366792,\"translated\":false},{\"author_name\":\"Mel anie\",\"author_url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/105120419714212330752\\/reviews\",\"language\":\"en\",\"original_language\":\"en\",\"profile_photo_url\":\"https:\\/\\/lh3.googleusercontent.com\\/a-\\/ALV-UjW3bdX18cT3ca7CK53AELZ06kU1KrCuIO4PNszK27RNjfgP=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\",\"rating\":4,\"relative_time_description\":\"a year ago\",\"text\":\"This place is okay if you manage your expectations. They had a limited menu, which is to be expected. The employees were nice, but the check out line was very, very, very slow. Thankful they had canned Bublys (and for $1.50).\",\"time\":1658778829,\"translated\":false},{\"author_name\":\"Dirk Johnson\",\"author_url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.google.com\\/maps\\/contrib\\/111146815649936945683\\/reviews\",\"language\":\"en\",\"original_language\":\"en\",\"profile_photo_url\":\"https:\\/\\/lh3.googleusercontent.com\\/a\\/ACg8ocKfjCmc8hT8RLEOn3G15d96pFPBR6Qt4CGuvEjQ2rPJ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\",\"rating\":5,\"relative_time_description\":\"2 months ago\",\"text\":\"I loved the saloon. Guy was great, so many good tips and a good beer. Prices are a little high but not bad really. Thanks for being open.\",\"time\":1687826731,\"translated\":false}],\"serves_breakfast\":true,\"serves_dinner\":true,\"serves_lunch\":true,\"takeout\":true,\"types\":[\"restaurant\",\"food\",\"point_of_interest\",\"establishment\"],\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/maps.google.com\\/?cid=15442152632363214466\",\"user_ratings_total\":21,\"utc_offset\":-420,\"vicinity\":\"6225 Arizona 67, North Rim\",\"website\":\"https:\\/\\/www.grandcanyonforever.com\\/dining\",\"wheelchair_accessible_entrance\":true}}',1,'2023-09-19 05:55:42','2023-09-19 05:5